  "summary": "The advertised pay of $20–$35 per hour for remote package work does appear in real job listings, so the rate itself is plausible. However, the job duties described — receiving, repackaging, and forwarding packages — match a pattern the FTC has repeatedly warned about: 'reshipping scams,' where people are unknowingly used as middlemen to move goods bought with stolen payment information. According to the FTC, real companies do not ask people to forward goods from their homes, and a job that consists only of reshipping packages is never a real job. Until you can confirm this offer through an official channel, don't send money or share any codes or personal details.",
